Open your GitHub Account and Click on Plus icon in the top tool bar and create New Repositary.
Give the Repository name
Choose whether you want to make the Repo Public (visible to anyone) or Private (only visible to you). Then click in Create Repository Button
Check the box that says Add a README File. It setups the repository with basic text file so no need to use any command lines to setup
Then Click in Create Repository 
Once repo is created, go to the repo and create a txt file.
Then commit changes
